        "description": "<p>Lately I've been testing frontier models by having them create self-contained web pages that display clocks--sort of my personal version of Simon Willison\u2019s pelican-on-a-bicycle metric.<p>I have been particularly impressed by the variety, interest, and quality of the clocks created by Claude Opus 5.5. Over the course of several sessions in the Claude chat interface, I had it build a total of 500 clocks.<p>Claude\u2019s summary of the prompting process and page design is here:<p><a href=\"https://github.com/tkgally/500-clocks/tree/main\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://github.com/tkgally/500-clocks/tree/main</a></p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50137820\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50137820</a></p>\n<p>Points: 37</p>\n<p># Comments: 9</p>",
